femto patch for quireink-stardict 0.3.0
Subject: validate entries while preparing the block index

While building the sparse index (Prepare::step):
- reject empty, over-long or non-UTF-8 headwords;
- reject entries that are out of order under the lookup comparison;
- for .syn files, reject targets outside the headword index
  (Kind::Synonyms now carries word_count);
- reject an index whose entry count is reached before the end of the file;
- once a step has failed, later steps return an error instead of resuming.

Dictionary::open also propagates a failure to open the declared synonym
index; upstream discarded that error and continued without synonyms.

Same motivation as 0002: reject malformed user-supplied dictionaries at
preparation time.

